  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Speculation regarding the resignation of Indonesian Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has surfaced following reports that he allegedly submitted a resignation letter to President Prabowo Subianto. This development follows legal challenges, including a Supreme Court ruling regarding his educational certificates, which has sparked parliamentary discussions concerning his tenure. While some reports suggest the potential submission of documentation to the People's Consultative Assembly, top legislative officials, including MPR Chairman Ahmad Muzani and Deputy House Speaker Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, have publicly stated that they have not received, seen, or confirmed any formal resignation papers. Official sources have expressed a lack of direct knowledge regarding these claims, noting that current information on the matter is derived primarily from media reports. The situation remains a subject of intense public interest and ongoing political discourse as institutional leaders continue to address the unverified reports emerging from various news outlets.",
